  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">First Economic Reform Support Operation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The First Economic Reform Support Development Policy Operation Project in the Kingdom of Tonga is the first in a series of two programmatic development policy operations that aims to improve the mobilization and use of public resources while addressing constraints to private sector development. This program focuses on three components, including public financial management, fiscal policy, and the business environment. The Government of Tonga will strengthen resource mobilization for improved public services and reforms to support sustainable job creation, a process reflecting a strong collaboration with the International Finance Corporation (IFC). Policy areas for the operation are: (i) strengthening public financial management; (ii) strengthening fiscal policy; and (iii) enhancing the business enabling environment. This first operation contributes mainly to the first theme of the country assistance strategy, supporting policy reform to strengthen economic growth prospects and improve service delivery. In addition, the policy actions and associated budget support will facilitate accumulation of cash reserves, contributing to the third theme of the country assistance strategy on building resilience against shocks. The main risks of the proposed operation and their associated mitigation strategies are capacity constraints, macroeconomic disruption, and political uncertainty.</narrative>
  </description>
